Ignore the application's GALLIUM_DRIVER in this private VA build.

Applications set GALLIUM_DRIVER for their own Mesa: Firefox on Mali VirGL needs
virpipe, and the Adreno desktop uses zink. This Mesa holds only freedreno, zink
and softpipe, and its software screen picker stops at the first driver named by
GALLIUM_DRIVER, so the Termux:VA software backend failed with "llvmpipe screen
creation failed" inside any such process. Read TERMUX_VA_GALLIUM_DRIVER
instead; unset, the picker falls back to softpipe as for other VA clients.

--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/target-helpers/sw_helper.h
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/target-helpers/sw_helper.h
@@ -74,7 +74,10 @@
 {
    UNUSED bool only_sw = debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE", false);
    const char *drivers[] = {
-      (sw_vk ? "" : debug_get_option("GALLIUM_DRIVER", "")),
+      /* Termux:VA: GALLIUM_DRIVER belongs to the application's own Mesa (virpipe, zink,
+       * llvmpipe), which this private VA build may lack; naming a missing driver here
+       * would stop the search. Only TERMUX_VA_GALLIUM_DRIVER selects one. */
+      (sw_vk ? "" : debug_get_option("TERMUX_VA_GALLIUM_DRIVER", "")),
 #if defined(GALLIUM_D3D12)
       (sw_vk || only_sw) ? "" : "d3d12",
 #endif
